<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Second Empire of Haiti</h1><p class="st-meta">1849 CE – 1859 CE · capital Port-au-Prince</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Haiti's second empire under Faustin I, a former soldier who crowned himself in imperial splendour and repeatedly failed to reconquer the Dominican Republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1847 the Haitian senate chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faustin-soulouque">Faustin Soulouque</a>, an elderly and supposedly pliable general, as president. He soon turned on the mixed-race elite who had promoted him, killing opponents in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-au-prince">Port-au-Prince</a> in 1848. On 26 August 1849 he had himself proclaimed emperor as Faustin I, and he was crowned with great ceremony in 1852.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faustin-soulouque">Faustin</a> created a court and nobility of princes, dukes and barons, ruled through the army and a feared militia, and tolerated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-vodou">Vodou</a> more openly than his predecessors. The state monopolised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> purchases, and the economy suffered. He invaded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-dominican-republic">First Dominican Republic</a> in 1849 and again in 1855 to 1856, but was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-carreras">Las Carreras</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-santome">Santomé</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sabana-larga">Sabana Larga</a>, which cost him prestige.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In December 1858 General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fabre-geffrard">Fabre Geffrard</a> rose in revolt, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faustin-soulouque">Faustin</a> abdicated in January 1859 and went into exile. Geffrard restored the presidency, founding the modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-haiti-1806-1849">Republic of Haiti</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/second-empire-of-haiti.jpg" alt="Second Empire of Haiti" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Baselle · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imperial_Flag_of_Haiti_(1849-1859).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1849 CE – 1859 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Port-au-Prince</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Faustin I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism and Vodou</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Haitian Creole and French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/haiti">Haiti</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Empire of Haiti (1849-1859)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1854&amp;focus=second-empire-of-haiti" aria-label="Second Empire of Haiti on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2721 1490 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Second Empire of Haiti lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3041 1746L3041 1746M3041 1746L3041 1746"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3041 1746h0M3041 1746h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3041 1746h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3041 1746h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Port-au-Prince. <a href="/atlas?year=1854&amp;focus=second-empire-of-haiti">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
